{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "פרי עץ", :translit "pri etz", :gloss "fruit of a tree"} {:he "אשר בו פרי עץ", :translit "asher bo pri etz", :gloss "in which is fruit of a tree"} {:he "פרי עץ הדר", :translit "pri etz hadar", :gloss "fruit of a majestic tree"} {:he "אתרוג", :translit "etrog", :gloss "etrog"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["פרי עץ" "פרי עץ הדר"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'fruit of a majestic tree' (Leviticus 23:40) is applied to the etrog because its wood tastes like its fruit. The Tree of Knowledge is identified as an etrog in the view that since Scripture says of all other trees 'fruit of a tree' (meaning the fruit, not the bark), the tree from which Adam ate must be one whose wood and fruit are identical — the etrog. The midrash records this identification in the name of Rabbi Meir.", :sources ["Talmud Sukkah 35a" "Bereshit Rabbah 15:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זכר", :translit "zakhar", :gloss "male"} {:he "ברכה", :translit "berakhah", :gloss "blessing"} {:he "נקיבה", :translit "nekeivah", :gloss "female"} {:he "בקללה", :translit "b'kelalah", :gloss "in curse"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זכר", :b "ברכה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "נקיבה", :b "בקללה"}], :frame {:text "The verse introduces the categories 'male and female' in the context of God's blessing (Genesis 1:27–28). The Targum renders 'male and female' with Aramaic terms 'דכר ונוקבא', and these terms are standard in rabbinic literature for the masculine and feminine principles.", :sources ["Genesis 1:27" "Targum Onkelos Genesis 1:27"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["פרי עץ" "פרי עץ הדר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "פרי עץ", :refs ["Genesis 1:29" "Leviticus 23:40"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "פרי עץ הדר", :refs ["Leviticus 23:40"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "זכר", :a-value 227, :b "ברכה", :b-value 227, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "נקיבה", :a-value 167, :b "בקללה", :b-value 167, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:03:51.945209229Z", :model "glm-5.2"}